WEBVTT

00:00:16.727 --> 00:00:20.772
ITIUSUU HO yume '(GHGGTGFU you I18

00:00:20.856 --> 00:00:24.735
<i>genjitsumi nado nai kotoba</i>

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:28.780
<i>soko ni yadoru mirai no katachi</i>

00:00:28.864 --> 00:00:38.248
<i>kasuka ni kagayaita hitomi ni</i>

00:00:40.459 --> 00:00:48.425
<i>guuzen mitai ni surechigau hibi tadotta</i>

00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:58.101
<i>deai ga hajimaru nani ka o madowasu kigen</i>

00:00:58.185 --> 00:01:02.606
<i>unmei ga waratte iru no? kikoeru</i>

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:06.151
<i>kousa suru kietsu to itami</i>

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:10.572
<i>ano hi tsugerareta koe ni kasumeru</i>

00:01:10.656 --> 00:01:14.201
<i>hyouri no tsuyosa o kakaeta</i>

00:01:14.284 --> 00:01:22.125
<i>ima wa tokenai wake o himo toite</i>

00:01:22.209 --> 00:01:32.719
<i>kaneta negai no sono saki e habataku</i>

00:01:50.737 --> 00:01:53.323
Would you want to, you know...

00:01:53.407 --> 00:01:55.784
...go out with me?

00:01:59.204 --> 00:02:00.580
Okay!

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:18.598
"Overture, Part 2 "

00:02:32.738 --> 00:02:34.322
Wow...

00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:37.784
Junko, going out with our
grade's biggest hunk...!

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:41.413
Yukio Hamaguchi
has good taste, though.

00:02:41.496 --> 00:02:43.832
He totally ignored all the
annoying girls who went after him.

00:02:43.915 --> 00:02:47.544
Junko's practically shining!

00:02:47.627 --> 00:02:50.797
Yeah, she had given
it up as a hopeless crush.

00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:04.811
What do you want to do?
Want to visit Joshi Park?

00:03:04.895 --> 00:03:08.190
Didn't you say they
sell great ice cream there?

00:03:08.273 --> 00:03:11.943
Yeah, I'd like some!

00:03:12.027 --> 00:03:14.321
Oh, you're wearing it!

00:03:14.404 --> 00:03:18.909
I know I should wear
it when I'm dressed nicer,

00:03:18.992 --> 00:03:21.328
but I just couldn't wait...

00:03:21.411 --> 00:03:26.666
I hope you like it. I wasn't
really sure if you would or not.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:30.670
I do. It's really pretty!

00:03:30.754 --> 00:03:32.923
But it must've been expensive...

00:03:33.006 --> 00:03:36.718
Oh, I guess I kind of went overboard,

00:03:36.802 --> 00:03:39.513
but all that matters is that you like it!

00:03:39.596 --> 00:03:43.016
Thanks. I'll treasure it.

00:03:45.102 --> 00:03:46.728
Oh, the light.

00:03:46.812 --> 00:03:48.188
Mm!

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:15.590
<i>A single flower quietly bloomed in
the shade of a tree, out of harm's way</i>

00:04:15.674 --> 00:04:25.600
<i>At some point the lie that it lived
there transformed into a truth</i>

00:04:25.684 --> 00:04:34.442
<i>Oh, I hope to be reborn</i>

00:04:34.526 --> 00:04:42.951
<i>If the light of the future
is deep inside your heart</i>

00:04:43.034 --> 00:04:49.916
<i>then let me get a little closer</i>

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:01.303
<i>because I want to reach
down there and rescue you</i>

00:05:01.386 --> 00:05:12.105
<i>If you're worried you'll forget,
then I'll connect our memories</i>

00:05:12.105 --> 00:05:13.648
This place is actually pretty fun, huh?

00:05:13.648 --> 00:05:20.238
<i>One by one</i>

00:05:20.238 --> 00:05:20.864
Yeah!

00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:29.039
<i>Reborn on this vast earth
(living again)</i>

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:29.706
Okay! Then the week after that, too!

00:05:29.706 --> 00:05:38.381
<i>Whenever you feel like you're being
buried or about to lose sight of things</i>

00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:39.966
--They're just around the corner!
--You're in a real rush!

00:05:39.966 --> 00:05:47.140
<i>Down to the tips of
those leaf veins (breathe)</i>

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:47.307
We will.

00:05:47.307 --> 00:05:55.148
<i>Bathe in the light and feel this breathing</i>

00:06:00.779 --> 00:06:11.581
<i>Because no one yet knows</i>

00:06:11.665 --> 00:06:19.923
<i>if the conclusion
we'll reach is true or not</i>

00:06:26.346 --> 00:06:27.722
Junko“.

00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:34.521
Do you consider that proper for a
high school student?! It's disgraceful!

00:06:34.604 --> 00:06:36.231
I haven't done anything disgraceful!

00:06:36.314 --> 00:06:40.235
It is disgraceful!
Going there after school and...

00:06:40.318 --> 00:06:43.780
You're not allowed to
see that creep ever again!

00:06:43.863 --> 00:06:46.324
Hamaguchi-kun is not a creep!

00:06:46.408 --> 00:06:49.369
It's obscene, parading around
with a girl while in a school uniform!

00:06:49.452 --> 00:06:52.122
How can you say that?! You don't
know anything about him!

00:06:52.205 --> 00:06:52.956
"Stop!

00:06:52.998 --> 00:06:54.457
“Let go!
"Stop!

00:07:01.131 --> 00:07:02.507
Junko!

00:07:13.518 --> 00:07:17.105
There's no information on
the Denizen to be had from this.

00:07:17.188 --> 00:07:22.569
It seems Junko Ogami was
devoured before she realized it after all.

00:07:23.445 --> 00:07:26.990
Yukio Hamaguchi said he met someone.

00:07:27.073 --> 00:07:30.076
It's possible he was the Denizen...

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.036
--Umm...

00:07:31.036 --> 00:07:31.828
--Huh?
--Umm...

00:07:31.911 --> 00:07:34.289
Sorry. I'll be just a minute.

00:07:34.372 --> 00:07:35.749
<i>Okay -</i>

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.801
Excuse me. Do you have a minute?

00:07:48.637 --> 00:07:51.640
I'm a photographer.

00:07:51.723 --> 00:07:55.310
I've been looking for a model like you.

00:07:55.393 --> 00:07:58.605
I'd like to photograph you,
if you don't mind.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.816
Huh?

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:07.989
I'd very much like to put a
handsome boy like you on film.

00:08:08.073 --> 00:08:09.532
--Very much.

00:08:09.532 --> 00:08:12.077
--I'm with someone, though...
--Very much.

00:08:15.455 --> 00:08:18.375
Just until your companion returns, then.

00:08:24.172 --> 00:08:27.008
He looks weird, but he seems legit.

00:08:27.092 --> 00:08:29.886
Guess it's okay
until Junko comes back...

00:08:29.969 --> 00:08:31.221
Okay, just a little bit.

00:08:31.304 --> 00:08:33.098
Thank you.

00:08:47.904 --> 00:08:50.698
Good. Very good.

00:08:59.249 --> 00:09:02.627
Thank you. I was able to
get some wonderful photographs.

00:09:02.710 --> 00:09:06.881
Are these photos going to
be in a magazine or something?

00:09:06.965 --> 00:09:08.299
Why, yes.

00:09:08.383 --> 00:09:10.677
What's the magazine's name?

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.597
Never mind that. Could you
model again for me tomorrow?

00:09:14.681 --> 00:09:18.059
But not in that uniform,
something more handsome...

00:09:18.601 --> 00:09:22.105
If you agree to it, then I'll give
you prints of these photographs

00:09:22.188 --> 00:09:24.733
and the next set as well.

00:09:24.816 --> 00:09:26.359
--Plus a little compensation.

00:09:26.359 --> 00:09:27.694
--Really?!
--Plus a little compensation.

00:09:27.777 --> 00:09:31.614
Oh, but I have school.
Next Saturday would be better...

00:09:31.698 --> 00:09:35.577
That will be fine.
Be sure to come next Saturday, then.

00:09:41.458 --> 00:09:45.795
And then when he
saw Junko Ogami after that...

00:09:45.879 --> 00:09:48.882
...she was already a Torch.

00:09:48.965 --> 00:09:53.678
He fits the place
and time to be the Denizen.

00:09:53.761 --> 00:09:58.641
The combination of a Crimson Denizen
and photographs is odd, though.

00:09:58.725 --> 00:10:01.311
There was once a Denizen
that lived solely to paint

00:10:01.394 --> 00:10:03.605
and left behind a skilled pupil.

00:10:03.688 --> 00:10:09.194
It would not be surprising for there
to be one that loves photographs.

00:10:09.277 --> 00:10:10.904
Mm.

00:10:10.987 --> 00:10:14.199
But I don't understand why
only Junko Ogami was devoured

00:10:14.282 --> 00:10:17.619
while Yukio Hamaguchi
was left unscathed.

00:10:17.702 --> 00:10:21.164
That American Torch is also a mystery.

00:10:21.247 --> 00:10:24.167
At any rate, tomorrow you
should meet with Yukio Hamaguchi

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.212
and this so-called
photographer to learn more.

00:10:46.105 --> 00:10:49.317
This has nothing to do with the Denizen.

00:10:56.616 --> 00:10:57.992
Junko.

00:10:59.244 --> 00:11:00.620
Wait.

00:11:04.916 --> 00:11:08.169
You should wear this if you're
going to see Hamaguchi-kun!

00:11:42.412 --> 00:11:43.329
--Shall we go?

00:11:43.329 --> 00:11:44.706
--Yeah.
--Shall we go?

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.799
I feel really good.

00:11:54.882 --> 00:11:58.636
Say, I should have that photographer
get a shot of us together!

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:04.559
I know there's a Denizen in this city,
but it's still staying inactive.

00:12:04.642 --> 00:12:09.731
I'm sure it senses me, but there's
no sign that it intends to fight

00:12:09.814 --> 00:12:12.650
or that it's devoured any more humans.

00:12:12.734 --> 00:12:15.361
Just what is it up to?

00:12:16.821 --> 00:12:17.739
What?

00:12:17.822 --> 00:12:20.742
Oh, no, you just have
this serious look on your face.

00:12:20.825 --> 00:12:23.411
I thought maybe you weren't having fun...

00:12:23.494 --> 00:12:25.204
Fun?

00:12:25.288 --> 00:12:28.249
You said you wanted
to meet the photographer...

00:12:28.333 --> 00:12:30.877
Have you changed your mind?
If so, I can go by myself--

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.253
No, I haven't.

00:12:32.337 --> 00:12:33.129
Really?

00:12:33.212 --> 00:12:35.173
I have to act normal.

00:12:35.256 --> 00:12:37.592
What would Junko Ogami have done?

00:12:37.675 --> 00:12:40.637
How would she have
cheered up Yukio Hamaguchi?

00:12:54.734 --> 00:12:56.110
Oh?

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:58.738
Isn't that...?

00:12:58.821 --> 00:13:01.616
My mother repaired it.

00:13:01.699 --> 00:13:05.620
Oh, you made up. I'm glad.

00:13:11.709 --> 00:13:14.087
Time to slay the Denizen...

00:13:30.895 --> 00:13:33.731
Let's see... Not here yet?

00:13:33.815 --> 00:13:35.817
--You mean the aforementioned photographer?

00:13:35.817 --> 00:13:37.026
--Aforementioned...?
--You mean the aforementioned photographer?

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:38.027
Yeah.

00:13:38.111 --> 00:13:40.697
He showed up out of the blue last time.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:44.909
But this was the spot.
Let's wait for a little bit.

00:13:44.993 --> 00:13:46.369
Mm.

00:13:48.621 --> 00:13:51.124
Was I spacing out far from here?

00:13:51.207 --> 00:13:53.584
Don't be silly. It was right there.

00:13:55.211 --> 00:13:59.007
Nearby. 15 or 16 meters, at most.

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.842
--I'll get us something to drink. What do you--

00:14:00.842 --> 00:14:02.802
--A beverage with a fruit juice in its name.
--I'll get us something to drink. What do you--

00:14:02.885 --> 00:14:05.680
One that has sweetener
and very little sourness.

00:14:05.763 --> 00:14:06.764
Huh? What?

00:14:06.848 --> 00:14:09.100
A sweet fruit juice.

00:14:09.183 --> 00:14:11.978
Okay. Just a minute.

00:14:13.187 --> 00:14:15.356
<i>What do you think, Master'?</i>

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:19.277
Mm. If the photographer is the Denizen,
then, given this close distance,

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:24.866
Yukio Hamaguchi was surely inside
the Seal too when it devoured her.

00:14:24.949 --> 00:14:27.702
The question is why
didn't it devour both of them...

00:14:27.785 --> 00:14:31.080
This opponent's a tough one, all right.

00:14:31.164 --> 00:14:34.333
A person's desires
can take infinite shapes.

00:14:34.417 --> 00:14:39.130
Denizens that can freely evince
those shapes are all the more varied.

00:14:39.213 --> 00:14:44.135
Do you think it'll come?
I don't sense anything at all...

00:14:44.218 --> 00:14:46.012
--Yukio Hamaguchi is gone!

00:14:46.012 --> 00:14:46.888
--What?!
--Yukio Hamaguchi is gone!

00:14:46.971 --> 00:14:50.057
How?! I only looked away for a few seconds!

00:14:50.141 --> 00:14:53.102
No human could do this. In which case...

00:14:59.942 --> 00:15:04.197
"Stack yard" "No trespassing"
"Joshi Park Reconstruction"

00:15:13.414 --> 00:15:16.626
No question about it!
A Crimson Denizen!

00:15:24.967 --> 00:15:30.306
How amateurish,
leaving behind such an awful trail!

00:15:30.389 --> 00:15:34.102
But I didn't sense anything,
despite it being so near!

00:15:34.185 --> 00:15:36.354
It must be a very low-level Denizen.

00:15:36.437 --> 00:15:42.318
To think that it would dare to abduct
someone in front of a Flame Haze...

00:15:42.401 --> 00:15:43.778
Damn.

00:15:44.654 --> 00:15:46.447
I'm such a fool.

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:05.091
--In there!

00:16:05.091 --> 00:16:06.008
--A vehicle?!
--In there!

00:16:06.092 --> 00:16:07.844
Why is it acting so simple-minded?!

00:16:07.927 --> 00:16:10.555
We can ask questions later!

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.135
A Seal?!

00:17:14.035 --> 00:17:17.330
What are these?

00:17:17.413 --> 00:17:19.290
It's "Flame-haired, Burning-eyed"...

00:17:19.373 --> 00:17:22.293
Damn, she's beautiful...

00:17:22.376 --> 00:17:26.297
Who are you?! What are you doing here?

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:31.886
And the actual Flame of
the Heavens, the Crimson God.

00:17:31.969 --> 00:17:34.472
I'll tell you. These all belong to me...

00:17:34.555 --> 00:17:36.682
...the great "Costumed Player" Ukobach.

00:17:36.766 --> 00:17:37.975
Ukobach?

00:17:38.059 --> 00:17:39.560
I've not heard of you.

00:17:39.644 --> 00:17:46.609
These are... These are models
for the form I will someday take.

00:17:53.658 --> 00:17:56.827
Manifestation of one's
true nature is rare these days.

00:17:56.911 --> 00:18:00.831
Th-This is not the form I desire.

00:18:00.915 --> 00:18:03.751
I am studying the forms
of those I've gathered here

00:18:03.834 --> 00:18:08.923
to create the most beautiful
form for myself someday.

00:18:09.006 --> 00:18:11.300
To create a satisfying form...

00:18:19.308 --> 00:18:22.520
You've been capturing humans for that?

00:18:22.603 --> 00:18:25.773
To create an outward appearance
that doesn't reflect your inner nature?

00:18:25.856 --> 00:18:29.860
That's right. Someday I will.
Someday it will happen.

00:18:29.944 --> 00:18:32.196
No, it won't. You're weak.

00:18:32.279 --> 00:18:33.114
What?!

00:18:33.197 --> 00:18:35.074
You caught me off guard

00:18:35.157 --> 00:18:38.744
because your power of existence,
as evidenced by your emotion and lust,

00:18:38.828 --> 00:18:41.956
was so miniscule that you blended
in with the ordinary humans.

00:18:45.584 --> 00:18:47.169
You're weak.

00:18:47.253 --> 00:18:51.007
Even if you create the form you want,
you'd be too weak to maintain it.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:53.342
And you know it.

00:19:00.975 --> 00:19:06.397
Even so, one who clings to "someday"
can only grow smaller and weaker.

00:19:17.825 --> 00:19:22.413
It's no use. Such cheap tricks
don't work on the Nietono no Shana.

00:19:22.496 --> 00:19:24.206
Now return to the Crimson World.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:28.294
A Denizen like you will
accomplish nothing in this world;

00:19:28.377 --> 00:19:30.338
you'll only cause harm.

00:19:31.005 --> 00:19:33.758
Recognize this one?

00:19:33.841 --> 00:19:37.136
He isn't dead. He's still alive.

00:19:37.219 --> 00:19:40.306
My Atalanta Treasure captures people.

00:19:40.389 --> 00:19:42.975
It confines them. That's all it can do.

00:19:43.059 --> 00:19:43.809
SQ?

00:19:43.851 --> 00:19:49.357
All of them. They all continue to live.
They just can't move.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:51.025
They continue to live?

00:19:51.108 --> 00:19:54.236
Then the man that
was found after ten years...

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:58.491
He got old and dirty,
so I devoured him and threw him away.

00:19:58.574 --> 00:20:02.078
To think I was discovered because
I left him a little power of existence...

00:20:02.161 --> 00:20:04.163
How unlucky.

00:20:04.246 --> 00:20:08.167
Was it wrong of me to make
this one dress up before I took him?

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:11.879
Or was devouring the girl who got
in the way of my photo shoot wrong too?

00:20:11.962 --> 00:20:14.090
Don't move. They're still alive.

00:20:14.173 --> 00:20:17.093
Do you honestly think a
Flame Haze cares about hostages?

00:20:17.176 --> 00:20:19.345
No, don't you understand?

00:20:19.428 --> 00:20:21.347
Imagine how much of a disturbance

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.974
devouring this many
living humans would create.

00:20:24.058 --> 00:20:25.184
Don't move!

00:20:25.267 --> 00:20:28.813
I'm going to display you
as a monument of my victory.

00:20:28.896 --> 00:20:30.856
Take this!

00:20:37.154 --> 00:20:39.365
Huh? Where'd she go?

00:20:58.425 --> 00:21:01.220
The confined humans remain unchanged.

00:21:01.303 --> 00:21:04.515
Not destroying the
Treasure was a wise decision.

00:21:13.107 --> 00:21:16.318
Not good. We're in a
moving vehicle. You must stop it.

00:21:16.402 --> 00:21:19.405
Urgh! It's a nuisance to the very end!

00:21:25.995 --> 00:21:27.371
Oh.

00:21:28.664 --> 00:21:30.749
It's already this late.

00:21:32.293 --> 00:21:35.421
I wonder how Junko's doing...

00:21:40.926 --> 00:21:44.180
I suppose she's at that age now.

00:21:45.723 --> 00:21:50.060
I wonder if he'd come if I invite him for tea.

00:21:50.144 --> 00:21:53.022
Getting to know him now
wouldn't be a bad idea, either.

00:21:54.523 --> 00:21:56.317
Because someday...

00:21:57.776 --> 00:21:59.612
I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:22:16.754 --> 00:22:20.925
Can anyone here speak Spanish?
No, err, Brazilian?

00:22:21.008 --> 00:22:22.176
--This one's an Italian!

00:22:22.176 --> 00:22:24.136
--Hydrate him! Anything will do!
--This one's an Italian!

00:22:25.221 --> 00:22:28.933
What's going on?
What happened to me?

00:22:33.646 --> 00:22:34.813
Junko“.

00:22:34.897 --> 00:22:36.982
Yeah, I was with Junko.

00:22:37.066 --> 00:22:38.859
Where is she?!

00:22:45.032 --> 00:22:47.993
That's a relief. She's all right.

00:22:57.586 --> 00:22:59.588
Junko...?

00:22:59.672 --> 00:23:01.048
Junko?

00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:04.969
Goodbye.

00:23:05.052 --> 00:23:07.721
Huh? Junko?

00:23:29.535 --> 00:23:33.247
I hope we stay together forever,
Hamaguchi-kun.

00:23:38.502 --> 00:23:42.131
What's... Why am I holding this?

00:23:53.517 --> 00:23:54.893
Huh?

00:23:56.729 --> 00:23:58.689
Why am l...?

00:24:00.482 --> 00:24:03.444
What's wrong? Are you in pain?

00:24:28.761 --> 00:24:32.097
This latest Denizen was a simple opponent.

00:24:32.181 --> 00:24:36.852
Yes. But the way it blended
in with people was troublesome.

00:24:41.565 --> 00:24:44.485
I am sure that your
wanderings will someday lead you

00:24:44.568 --> 00:24:47.821
to someone who will
accept you just as you are.

00:24:47.905 --> 00:24:51.659
I think that would just be bothersome.

00:24:53.410 --> 00:24:58.707
I hope I'll get to fight something
tougher next time, like a Crimson Lord.

00:24:58.791 --> 00:25:00.167
Mm.

00:25:02.086 --> 00:25:03.462
Oto...

00:25:04.338 --> 00:25:06.548
And beyond it, Misaki...

00:25:24.733 --> 00:25:30.739
yuzurenakatta om oi idaki

00:25:30.823 --> 00:25:36.829
<i>sore demo koko made aruite kita</i>

00:25:36.912 --> 00:25:44.378
<i>susumete nai you de toki
no nami ni hakobareta</i>

00:25:44.461 --> 00:25:50.300
<i>negai ni sukoshi fureta</i>

00:25:50.384 --> 00:25:56.557
<i>tooi kioku o tadoru</i>

00:25:56.640 --> 00:26:06.942
<i>“kou ja nakatta" koto de
kagayaiteta ki ga shite</i>

00:26:07.025 --> 00:26:14.575
<i>mabushikatta ano hi o koe</i>

00:26:14.658 --> 00:26:16.869
<i>ima koko ni iru</i>

00:26:16.952 --> 00:26:26.879
<i>owari toka hajimari toka
doko demo nai kono basho de</i>

00:26:26.962 --> 00:26:29.256
<i>kore kara bokura</i>

00:26:29.339 --> 00:26:41.226
<i>mata aruki arata na yume
mitsuke dasu koto darou</i>

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:05.375
And then, here in Misaki City, we met.

00:27:11.924 --> 00:27:16.303
We went on to
have numerous intense battles...

00:27:22.518 --> 00:27:25.687
...and many other things as well.

00:27:40.327 --> 00:27:43.288
...Until we parted ways on that day.

00:28:09.523 --> 00:28:11.316
We'll meet again...

00:28:20.075 --> 00:28:21.660
<i>- . .Y !</i>
